    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0819" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/589</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shea</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-26T12:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 26, 1918, 12 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 27, 4.30
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Unofficial report that Government has ordered Chilean naval crews to take
                    possession of all [interned] German boats.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d698-f1"/> At
                    Valparaiso order is being executed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shea</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d698-f1" n="2" xml:id="d698-f1-content">
                <p>See also the Ambassador’s telegram of Nov. 4, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg738">p. 738</ref>.</p>
            </note>
